      "writtenOn": "2022-07-14T06:56:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think of that RFC4429(Optimistic Duplicate Address Detection (DAD) for IPv6) defines an optimistic mode to skip the DAD and use the global IPv6 addresses directly. Looks like it\u0027s been supported in kernel for many years.\n\nI\u0027m wondering if we can have IFA_F_OPTIMISTIC flag associated to the assigned IPv6 address when create LinkAddress instances, then kernel should skip the DAD automatically for these IPv6 addresses. For test, apparently we don\u0027t care if there is indeed duplicate address conflict happened,",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "41dfaca8cfbdc1024fe1c826e36c7d23c7947d4f",
